{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XWgL4xScN9NbHdqdW29JEW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. go-unix-utils derives specs from C source code, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract, specify, synthesize, verify) with shared infrastructure:\n- `pkg/testutils/` — Differential testing harness (Go binary vs. GNU reference)\n- `pkg/sys/` — Platform syscall abstractions (terminal size, signals, file metadata)\n- `pkg/format/` — Output formatting (column alignment, ANSI colors, human-readable sizes)\n- `cmd/<utility>/` — Per-utility Go implementations with differential tests\n- `magefiles/` — Build targets wrapping build, lint, stats, orchestrator\n\n**Current State**: Foundation packages are complete with implementations and tests:\n- DONE: pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format (all have implementation + tests on working branch)\n- NOT STARTED: magefiles (rel00.0-uc001), cmd/ts (rel01.0), cmd/wc, cmd/cat, cmd/sponge (rel01.1), cmd/du (rel02.0)\n- DEFERRED: cmd/ls (rel99.0, rel99.1)\n\n**Current Release**: rel00.0 has uc001-magefiles remaining; rel01.0 (ts) is the next utility release.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nThe foundation (rel00.0 uc002–004) is complete. The remaining rel00.0 item is magefiles, whose most critical targets (cobbler:measure, cobbler:stitch) depend on the external mage-claude-orchestrator library, while basic targets (build, lint) can be run directly via Go tooling.\n\nThe most impactful next step is **cmd/ts** (rel01.0-uc001) — the first utility. It validates the full pipeline from specification to differential testing, exercises the foundation packages (pkg/sys for SIGPIPE, pkg/testutils for verification), and is the simplest utility in the roadmap (moreutils timestamp prepend). Per P2, implementation and tests are split; this task covers implementation only.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"rel01.0-uc001 ts: Implement cmd/ts timestamp prepend utility\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (project structure, cmd/ package layout, design decisions)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd004-ts.yaml (ts utility PRD; if this path is incorrect, locate the ts PRD in docs/specs/product-requirements/ matching prd*-ts.yaml)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.0-uc001-ts.yaml (ts use case with end-to-end execution flow)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-01.0.yaml (test suite defining inputs and expected outputs)\n      - pkg/sys/signal.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler API for pipeline signal handling)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/ts/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"ts utility entry point: reads stdin line-by-line, prepends formatted timestamps, writes to stdout\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Read stdin line-by-line and write each line to stdout with a formatted timestamp prepended, as specified in the ts utility PRD\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Support the default timestamp format and a custom strftime-compatible format string passed as a positional argument, as specified in the ts utility PRD\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Support -s flag (elapsed time since program start) and -i flag (incremental time since last line) for relative timestamp modes, as specified in the ts utility PRD\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Install SIGPIPE handler via pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at startup and exit with correct codes (0 on success, non-zero on error), as specified in the ts utility PRD\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main() for pipeline SIGPIPE behavior, per prd002-sys R3.1 and R3.2\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Single cmd/ts/main.go file per ARCHITECTURE.yaml convention: each cmd/ sub-package contains main.go for the implementation\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/ts/ compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"echo 'hello' | go run ./cmd/ts/ prepends a timestamp to the output line in the default format\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"All flags specified in the ts PRD (-s, -i, custom format string) produce correct timestamp output\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Binary exits 0 on normal EOF and handles SIGPIPE cleanly without error output when stdout is closed\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":44883,"cache_read_input_tokens":19292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":44883},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"04409424-1c54-4408-9384-34d46d893b9f","uuid":"f75ecd44-603f-4eea-b927-8531e3ae1cb6"}
